From: Uke Linux contributors <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: preserve Cliffs proxy and stop ownership

Port the project two/three-rail proxy ownership from 52bbf80 and keep failed
voltage/load releases pending. Preserve primary/DTB PAS errors and completed
stop phases so retries cannot unmap or release a running processor's resources.
Reject another boot while a partial stop still owns resources.

Use the optional early-stop hook only for the Cliffs three-rail CDSP contract.
Other PAS targets retain their existing subdevice ordering. No new CDSP match,
firmware assignment or remoteproc activation is added. Startup-failure,
forced-removal and exported-DMA lifetimes still require separate validation.

Compared with exact Uke OEM 5712080a4b0c0b1a879e6d145c601c649ddaddfd,
OnePlus fc892483f1d61f245924681eb5abd563564d9cba and signed Linux 7.3.
Retain upstream Linux/Qualcomm GPL attribution.

